###### The seasonal component in focus  {#sec-sp-pastoral}   
In this livelihood system, the seasonal pattern mirrors that observed in @sec-sp-national, with a few key differences. It underwent a shift as of 2022.




```{r}
#| label: fig-seasonal-pattern-pastoral
#| fig-cap: "A glance at the seasonality of admissions in the pastoral livelihood system"
seasonal_cmpnt_pastoral
```




Before 2022, it used to exhibit three peaks: one high peak in June. A short duration, however, with a higher and sharper amplitude. Thereafter, a second peak, and relatively longer, between September and November and then another short peak in January (@fig-seasonal-pattern-pastoral-b2022). 

Regarding nadirs, during this period, there were two nadirs, both at almost the same level in terms of depth, though different in their duration. The first nadir was observed in April, and the second was between July and August.

As of 2022, the pattern changes: two high peaks are observed. The first and the shortest, in terms of duration, is observed between May and June. The second, and the long-lasting, between October and January of the following year (@fig-seasonal-pattern-pastoral-a2022). 

As for nadir, two nadirs are observed: a lower one (high depth), and shorter, in April. A second, but shallower and long-lasting between July and September.

::: {.panel-tabset}
