<br> 

###### The seasonal component in focus  
In this livelihood system, the seasonal pattern also mirrors those described in @sec-sp-national by far. Likewise, it has also suffered a shift that is exhibited as of 2022.




```{r}
#| label: fig-seasonal-pattern-agropastoral
#| fig-cap: "A glance at the seasonality of admissions in the agropastoral livelihood system"
seasonal_cmpnt_agropastoral
```




Before 2022, it used to exhibit one high peak between May and June, with a short duration, however, with a higher and sharper amplitude (@fig-seasonal-pattern-agropastoral-b2022). As of 2022, the pattern changes: two high peaks are observed. The first and the long-lasting is observed between May and August, and a second, and short-lasting, peak is observed between December and January (@fig-seasonal-pattern-agropastoral-a2022). 

As for nadir, there are two of them. The lowest nadir (with high depth) is observed between February and April, with the latter month being the one when the highest depth is observed, and has always been observed before and after 2022. A second nadir, with a shallow depth, is observed between September and November.

::: {.panel-tabset}
